# ARK Mobile Workflow Doctrine

Full doc: `docs/mobile/ark-mobile-workflow-doctrine.md`

## Identity

ARK Mobile is a **workflow engine**, not a miniature desktop and not a CRUD screen collection.

Every screen answers: **What does the user need to do next?** — not "What data do we have?"

## Build order

Complete **vertical workflows** before adding horizontal features:

1. Check-in → RO → assign technician
2. Inspection → concern workspace → finding (evidence) → recommendation → photos → complete
3. Comms → estimate → approval → payment (inline actions, no workspace hop)
4. Repair complete → pickup → close

If a step forces desktop, **observe why** — do not auto-build enforcement or new authority.

## Technician

Assume standing beside the vehicle. **Camera-first.** Concerns are workspaces — findings, photos, recommendations, discussion in one place. No "navigate to Finding Detail" thinking.

## Advisor

Comms actions inline: call, text, open RO, send estimate/payment/inspection, internal note — without leaving conversation.

## My Work cards

Pressure + next action, not status alone. Use projection fields (`next_action`, `attention_reason`, `age_label`, `primary_concern_id`). Tap → concern workspace when possible.

## Check-in

VIN → plate → existing customer → manual. Under one minute. Forms are fallback.

## Notifications

Interruptions → deep link to work. Not inboxes. Poll-first; push deferred per `ark-mobile-notification-doctrine.mdc`.

## Tablet

Master/detail, split view, persistent concern/findings/comms — less navigation when width allows.

## Guardrails

Authority → Observation → Projection → Configuration → Transport.

Flutter projection only. No parallel authority. No duplicated business logic. No shop-specific branching. Config in Settings.

## Success

User completes a visit without wondering where to go next. Hesitation or desktop reach = observation for roadmap.

